## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to implement streaming statistics with efficient data structures and real-time median calculation.

## Key Concepts

- Dual heap structure (max-heap + min-heap)
- Balance invariant maintenance
- Median computation in O(log n) per insert
- Streaming data processing

## Code Example

```javascript
class MedianStream {
  constructor() {
    this.low = new MaxHeap();  // Lower half
    this.high = new MinHeap(); // Upper half
  }

  insert(x) {
    // Insert into appropriate heap and rebalance
    if (this.low.isEmpty() || x <= this.low.peek()) {
      this.low.push(x);
    } else {
      this.high.push(x);
    }

    // Rebalance to maintain size difference ≤ 1
    if (this.low.size() > this.high.size() + 1) {
      this.high.push(this.low.pop());
    } else if (this.high.size() > this.low.size() + 1) {
      this.low.push(this.high.pop());
    }
  }

  getMedian() {
    if (this.low.size() > this.high.size()) {
      return this.low.peek();
    } else if (this.high.size() > this.low.size()) {
      return this.high.peek();
    } else {
      return (this.low.peek() + this.high.peek()) / 2;
    }
  }
}
```

## Implementation Notes

- Duplicates are handled naturally by heap properties
- Memory usage is O(n) for storing all elements
- Suitable for real-time streaming applications
- Can be extended to support removal operations with additional bookkeeping

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests mastery of rope-like data structures for dynamic sequences with cut-paste operations while maintaining fast range queries.

## Key Concepts

- **Implicit treap / rope**: Uses position as the key rather than explicit values
- **Split and merge operations**: Fundamental primitives for manipulating segments
- **Augmented data**: size and range sum maintained at each node
- **Edge cases**: Properly handling when dest overlaps with [l, r]

## Code Example

```javascript
class Node {
  constructor(v) {
    this.v = v;
    this.pr = Math.random();
    this.l = this.r = null;
    this.sz = 1;
    this.sum = v;
  }
}

function upd(t) {
  if (!t) return;
  t.sz = 1 + sz(t.l) + sz(t.r);
  t.sum = t.v + sum(t.l) + sum(t.r);
}

function split(t, k, l, r) {
  if (!t) return [null, null];
  if (sz(t.l) >= k) {
    let [a, b] = split(t.l, k, l, r);
    t.l = b; upd(t);
    return [a, t];
  } else {
    let [a, b] = split(t.r, k - sz(t.l) - 1, l, r);
    t.r = a; upd(t);
    return [t, b];
  }
}

function merge(a, b) {
  if (!a || !b) return a || b;
  if (a.pr < b.pr) {
    a.r = merge(a.r, b); upd(a); return a;
  } else {
    b.l = merge(a, b.l); upd(b); return b;
  }
}

function rangeSum(t, l, r) {
  let [a, bc] = split(t, l);
  let [b, c] = split(bc, r - l + 1);
  let res = sum(b);
  t = merge(a, merge(b, c));
  return res;
}

function moveSegment(t, l, r, dest) {
  let len = r - l + 1;
  let [a, bc] = split(t, l);
  let [b, c] = split(bc, len);
  t = merge(a, c);

  let pos = dest <= l ? dest : dest - len;
  let [x, y] = split(t, pos);\n  return merge(merge(x, b), y);
}
```

